<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">B. R. Ambedkar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bhimrao Ramji Ambedkar, Babasaheb Ambedkar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">B. R. Ambedkar was an Indian jurist, economist and social reformer who chaired the drafting committee of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a>. Born into the Mahar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a>, then treated as untouchable, he studied at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columbia-university">Columbia University</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> School of Economics with a scholarship from the ruler of Baroda, and campaigned against caste discrimination. He was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first law minister from 1947 to 1951, and shortly before his death converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> with hundreds of thousands of followers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/b-r-ambedkar.jpg" alt="B. R. Ambedkar" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dr._Bhimrao_Ambedkar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
